  "note": "Run each page's two sides for both themes (theme: light, then dark). The mirror's static examples are the server render, before the component's first measurement; the sketches (data-sketch sections) carry the measured states, so the geist marker reads roots inside them only. Ours measures on mount, so its base examples read as the at-rest sketches and its scripted examples as the scrolled ones, in the same order. A second run of the scroller page with the same configuration at a 600px viewport (page: scroller-narrow, both tabs resized) exercises the mobile-grid media rule: its only hard line is the grid tracks (1fr 1fr resolved against the stage width, 276px on the 552px sketch stage and 259px in ours), a stage-width difference like the soft widths.",
